1852	2010	1849	1849	he	110	" what a shameful coward , what a negative wretch , I have become by this one grief of my manhood ! An indifferent son , a careless brother , a useless , purposeless creature , content to dawdle away my life in feeble pottering with political economy . Shall I ever be in earnest again ? Is this dreary doubt of every living creature to go with me to my grave ? Less than two years ago my heart sickened at the thought that I had lived to two - and - thirty years of age , and had never been loved . Since then -- since then -- since then I had lived through life 's brief fever ; I have fought manhood 's worst and sharpest battle , and find myself -- where ? Exactly where I was before ; still companionless upon the dreary journey ; only a little nearer to the end . "
